,"lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to shift","definition_en":"μετα-κινέω, -ῶ \n [in LXX: Deu.19:14 (סוּג hi.), Isa.54:10 (מוֹט), etc. ;] \ntrans., \n to move away, remove (ὅρια, Deu, l.with). Mid., to remove oneself, remove, shift: metaphorically, ἀπὸ τ. ἐλπίδος, Col.1:23.†\n (AS)","source_line":3447}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"afastais","count":1}]},"G3474":{"id":"G3474","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3474","disambiguated_id":"G3474 =","unique_id":"G3474","headword":"μωρός","transliteration":"mōros","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"foolish","definition_en":"μωρός, -ά, -όν \n [in LXX for נָבָל, etc.; frequently in Sir. ;] \n__1. prop., of the nerves, dull, sluggish (Hipp., Arist.). \n __2. Of the mind, dull, stupid, foolish: Mat.5:22 (see Field, Notes, 3 ff.) Mat.7:26 23:17, 19 (T, WH, txt., R, om.) Mat.25:2-3, 8, 1Co.3:18 4:10; of things, παράδοσις, Mrk.7:13 (T, WH, txt., R, om.) : ζητήσεις, 2Ti.2:23, Tit.3:9; τὸ μ. τ. θεοῦ, 1Co.1:25; τὰ μ. τ. κόσμου, 1Co.1:27.†\n (AS)","source_line":3587}],"occurrence_count":12,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"tolas","count":5},{"gloss":"louco","count":2},{"gloss":"tolo","count":1},{"gloss":"tolos","count":1},{"gloss":"loucura","count":1},{"gloss":"loucas","count":1},{"gloss":"loucos","count":1}]},"G3601":{"id":"G3601","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3601","disambiguated_id":"G3601 =","unique_id":"G3601","headword":"ὀδύνη","transliteration":"odunē","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"anguish","definition_en":"ὀδύνη, -ης, ἡ \n [in LXX for יָגוֹן, מַר, etc. (26 words in all) ;] \npain, distress, of body or mind : Rom.9:2, 1Ti.6:10.†\n (AS)","source_line":3715}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"tormento","count":1},{"gloss":"com-dores","count":1}]},"G3752":{"id":"G3752","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3752","disambiguated_id":"G3752 =","unique_id":"G3752","headword":"ὅταν","transliteration":"hotan","lexical_morphology":"G:CONJ","gloss_en":"when(-ever)","definition_en":"ὅταν (for ὅτ᾽ ἄν = ὅτε ἄν), \n temporal particle, \nwith a conditional sense, usually of things expected to occur in an indefinite future; \n__1. prop., whenever; \n__(a) (a) with subjc. praes.: Mat.6:2, 5 Mrk.14:7, Luk.11:36, Jhn.7:27, Act.23:35, 1Co.3:4, al.; ἕως τ. ἡμέρας ἐκείνης, ὅ., Mat.26:29, Mrk.14:25; before τότε, 1Th.5:3; \n __(b) with subjc. aor. (M, Pr., 185): Mat.5:11, Mrk.4:15, Luk.6:22, Jhn.2:10 8:28 (Field, Notes, 94), 10:4, al. \n __2. As in Hom. (LS, see word), but not in cl. prose, with indic., when (M, Pr., 167f.; Bl., §65, 9): with impf., Mrk.3:11(cf. Gen.38:9, al.); with praes., Mrk.11:25; with fut.. Rev.4:9 (Swete, in l.); with aor., Mrk.11:19, Rev.8:1 (Swete, in ll.; M, Pr., 168, 248; Field, Notes, 35). \n (AS)","source_line":3869}],"occurrence_count":123,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"quando","count":120},{"gloss":"depois","count":3}]},"G3971":{"id":"G3971","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3971","disambiguated_id":"G3971 =","unique_id":"G3971","headword":"πατρῷος","transliteration":"patrōos","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"ancestral","definition_en":"πατρῷος, -α, -ον\n (πατήρ), [in LXX: Pro.27:10 (אָב), Est.7:5, 2 -4Ma.12:1-19 * ;] \nof one's fathers, received from one's fathers: Act.22:3 24:14 28:17.†\n (AS)","source_line":4089}],"occurrence_count":3,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"paterna","count":1},{"gloss":"pais","count":1},{"gloss":"pátrios","count":1}]},"G4156":{"id":"G4156","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4156","disambiguated_id":"G4156 =","unique_id":"G4156","headword":"πνικτός","transliteration":"pniktos","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"strangled","definition_en":"πνικτός, -ή, -όν\n (πνίγω), \nstrangled : Act.15:20, 29 21:25 (cf. Lev.17:13-14).†\n (AS)","source_line":4282}],"occurrence_count":3,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"carne-sufocada","count":3}]},"G4259":{"id":"G4259","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_i